test.yaml:17:31: untrusted input from the output of "gh pr view --json title" is written to $GITHUB_ENV. an attacker who controls the value can set LD_PRELOAD or NODE_OPTIONS (a newline adds another variable) and run code in the next steps. do not write input that an outsider controls to $GITHUB_ENV; validate it first, or pass it to the next step with $GITHUB_OUTPUT (only a value without line breaks, or one between a delimiter that nobody can guess, is safe there: see output-clobbering) [github-env]
test.yaml:19:11: untrusted input from the output of "gh pr view --json headRefName" is run as shell code by "eval". an attacker who controls the value can run any command in this step: a ; or $(...) in it is enough. do not run input that an outsider controls; pass it to the program as data, or validate it against a fixed list or a strict pattern first [command-injection]
test.yaml:22:11: untrusted input from the output of "gh api repos/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/pulls/$NUM --jq .user.name" is run as shell code by "eval". an attacker who controls the value can run any command in this step: a ; or $(...) in it is enough. do not run input that an outsider controls; pass it to the program as data, or validate it against a fixed list or a strict pattern first [command-injection]
test.yaml:24:29: untrusted input from the output of "gh api repos/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/pulls/$NUM --jq .body" is written to $GITHUB_OUTPUT as the record "body=..." and can hold a line break: an attacker who controls it ends the record and adds others, so it sets the other outputs of the step (steps.pr.outputs.*) that later steps trust. write a value without line breaks (validate it, or cut it down with tr -d '\n'), or write it between a delimiter that nobody can guess (delimiter=$(uuidgen); echo "body<<$delimiter" ...; echo "$delimiter") [output-clobbering]
test.yaml:41:27: untrusted input from the output of "git log --format" is written to $GITHUB_ENV. an attacker who controls the value can set LD_PRELOAD or NODE_OPTIONS (a newline adds another variable) and run code in the next steps. do not write input that an outsider controls to $GITHUB_ENV; validate it first, or pass it to the next step with $GITHUB_OUTPUT (only a value without line breaks, or one between a delimiter that nobody can guess, is safe there: see output-clobbering) [github-env]
test.yaml:43:11: untrusted input from the output of "git diff" is expanded into the command string of "bash -c", which the shell then parses as code: a value with shell syntax (a ;, a quote or $(...)) runs commands in this step. pass the value as an argument of the command string instead (bash -c 'cmd "$1"' _ "$VALUE"), or validate it against a fixed list or a strict pattern first [command-injection]
